  For settled-closed → keep the successor: the target is rejected; the successor stays live (S185>S145, S570-S574, S648-S651: successor mined, target rejected). R68-M6 says these are keep-successor, NOT keep-reject — the trap actually hit in round 68.

  For settled-split → narrow the scope: both rows mined; each keeps its scope; the successor's teaches must carry the limiter; if the limiter is missing the chain reads pending → add the limiter ("narrow the scope") or retire. Live example S575>S420.

  For pending → decide the ruling: the five-way ruling choice, then apply mechanism (repoint/usedby-flip/cell-flip/none per docstring: "mechanism is free text naming the settlement step (repoint, usedby-flip, cell-flip, none)").

